<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valentina Visconti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1368–1408</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Valentina Visconti, Duchess of Orléans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valentina Visconti was a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gian-galeazzo-visconti">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</a>, ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, who married Louis, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vi-of-france">Charles VI of France</a>, in 1389. Her marriage contract named her as heir to Milan if the male Visconti line failed. Her grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france">Louis XII of France</a> used this claim to conquer the duchy in 1499, drawing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> deeper into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valentina-visconti.jpg" alt="Valentina Visconti" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Honoré Bovet (text); Maître du Policratique de Charles V (images) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Honor%C3%A9_Bovet,_Apparicion_maistre_Jehan_de_Meun,_Valentina_Visconti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
